<title>LITHUANIA: BOURSE CAPITALISATION SLIGHTLY DOWN.</title>
<headline>BOURSE CAPITALISATION SLIGHTLY DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse fell slightly to 5.675 billion litas last week</p>
<p>versus 5.697 billion litas the previous five days, the national</p>
<p>stock exchange said on Monday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					     April 14-18   April 07-11</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		   15,048	  13,697</p>
<p>    Executed orders		    1,152	   1,580</p>
<p>Number of transaction on</p>
<p>    central market (CM)		1,058	   1,405</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL	17,249,520    11,534,000</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    bloc trades (BT)		   47		88</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	    4,715,050     21,677,020</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week	47,338,930    39,457,808</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week	3,943,911     4,083,278</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	    4,286,410     7,292,490</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	    4,715,050     19,654,910</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T bills	    14		17</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	  12,963,110    6,263,620</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
